# Requests for the API sent to the website. aisense.no has nothing under /services, so every
# path below it answers 404, and this sends that 404 to services/index.php, which answers with
# a short JSON note naming the API host instead of the HTML error page; a 403 for the folder
# itself goes there too. Nothing is redirected: the API keeps one address per endpoint. Only
# ErrorDocument is used, which AllowOverride FileInfo allows, as in the site's own .htaccess.
ErrorDocument 404 /services/index.php
ErrorDocument 403 /services/index.php
